    "bookTitle": "Amos",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 7,
    "summary": "Amos relates how he was called of God to be a prophet—He prophesies the captivity of Israel.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Thus hath the Lord God shewed unto me; and, behold, he formed grasshoppers in the beginning of the shooting up of the latter growth; and, lo, it was the latter growth after the king’s mowings.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 142,
            "end": 148
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Amos 7:1",
        "book": "Amos",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass, that when they had made an end of eating the grass of the land, then I said, O Lord God, forgive, I beseech thee: by whom shall Jacob arise? for he is small.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 25
          },
          {
            "start": 169,
            "end": 171
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Amos 7:2",
        "book": "Amos",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "The Lord repented for this: It shall not be, saith the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3,
            "text": "JST Amos 7:3 And the Lord said, concerning Jacob, Jacob shall repent for this, therefore I will not utterly destroy him, saith the Lord."
          },
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 17,
            "text": "Gen. 6:6; Num. 23:19."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
